The viral etiology of cervical cancer</article-title><source>Virus Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>189</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Virus Res||89|183||bib7|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12445658</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Castellsague</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>D&#x000ed;az</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>de Sanjos&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Mu&#x000f1;oz</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Herrero</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Franceschi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Peeling</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashley</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Snijders</surname><given-names>PJF</given-names></name><name><surname>Meijer</surname><given-names>CJLM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bosch</surname><given-names>FX</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Worldwide human papillomavirus etiology of cervical adenocarcinoma and its cofactors: implications for screening and prevention</article-title><source>J Natl Cancer Inst</source><year>2006</year><volume>98</volume><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>315</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Natl Cancer Inst||98|303||bib8|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16507827</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Castro</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Heiden</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Tribukait</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Preparation of cell nuclei from fresh tissues for high-quality DNA flow cytometry</article-title><source>Cytometry</source><year>1993</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>793</fpage><lpage>804</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cytometry||14|793||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8243208</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clifford</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Aguado</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Franceschi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of HPV type distribution in high-grade cervical lesions and cervical cancer: a meta-analysis</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2003</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>101</fpage><lpage>105</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||89|101||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12838308</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dahlgren</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Mellin</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Wangsa</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Heselmeyer-Haddad</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Bjornestal</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindholm</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Munck-Wikland</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Auer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Ried</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Dalianis</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparative genomic hybridization analysis of tonsillar cancer reveals a different pattern of genomic imbalances in human papillomavirus-positive and -negative tumors<